            <div xml:id="d564">

                <pb facs="0771" n="681" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg681"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.9411/33: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-05-21T14:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 21, 1920—2
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 4:10 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>833. It is practical in my opinion to bring to the attention of the Foreign
                    Office in an informal way the suggestions made in your 471, May 10, noon. I
                    think it best not to try to hurry in this matter but I will present it when a
                    good opportunity is offered.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
